# Allow the transformers.js native image dep (sharp) to run its build script on a
# clean install. pnpm >=10 blocks dependency build scripts by default.
#
# This .npmrc opts sharp in on pnpm versions that honor the setting. On pnpm
# versions where it isn't picked up, run once:
#     pnpm approve-builds --all     (or: pnpm rebuild sharp)
# See INTEGRATE.md §(e).
#
# Note: sharp is an OPTIONAL transitive dep of @xenova/transformers used only for
# IMAGE inputs — not for text. But TEXT embedding (all we use) is NOT dependency-free:
# transformers.js EAGERLY loads the native ONNX runtime (onnxruntime-node) on the first
# embed, so that native build MUST succeed or embedding fails and retrieval silently
# degrades to keyword-only. npm runs the native build scripts by default (over a clean
# tree); pnpm >=10 blocks them — which is exactly why install-model.mjs falls back to
# npm. (Building sharp only silences its optional load-time warning.)
onlyBuiltDependencies[]=sharp
